{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"fetch","tool":"fetch","arguments":{"max_length":12000,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Third_inauguration_of_Luiz_In%C3%A1cio_Lula_da_Silva"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Contents of https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Third_inauguration_of_Luiz_In%C3%A1cio_Lula_da_Silva:\nFrom Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\n2023 presidential inauguration of Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva\n\n|  |  |\n| --- | --- |\n|  | |\n| Date | 1 January 2023; 3 years ago |\n| Time | 15:00 ([BRT](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time_in_Brazil#Bras%C3%ADlia_time_(UTC%E2%88%9203:00) \"Time in Brazil\"), UTC−03:00) |\n| Location | * [National Congress of Brazil](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Congress_of_Brazil \"National Congress of Brazil\") [Brasília](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bras%C3%ADlia \"Brasília\"), [DF](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Federal_District_(Brazil) \"Federal District (Brazil)\") |\n| Participants | * [Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luiz_In%C3%A1cio_Lula_da_Silva \"Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva\") * 35th and 39th president of Brazil * *— Assuming office* * [Geraldo Alckmin](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geraldo_Alckmin \"Geraldo Alckmin\") * 26th vice president of Brazil * *— Assuming office* * [Rodrigo Pacheco](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rodrigo_Pacheco_(politician) \"Rodrigo Pacheco (politician)\") * [President of the Federal Senate](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_the_Federal_Senate_(Brazil) \"President of the Federal Senate (Brazil)\") * *— Administering oath* * [Arthur Lira](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arthur_Lira \"Arthur Lira\") * [President of the Chamber of Deputies](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_the_Chamber_of_Deputies_(Brazil) \"President of the Chamber of Deputies (Brazil)\") * *— Administering oath* * [Rosa Weber](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosa_Weber \"Rosa Weber\") * [President of the Supreme Federal Court](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supreme_Federal_Court#President_and_Vice_President \"Supreme Federal Court\") * *— Administering oath* |\n| ← [2019](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inauguration_of_Jair_Bolsonaro \"Inauguration of Jair Bolsonaro\")  *[2027](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Brazilian_general_election \"2026 Brazilian general election\")* → | |\n\n**Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva** and **Geraldo Alckmin** were inaugurated as [39th](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_presidents_of_Brazil \"List of presidents of Brazil\") [president of Brazil](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_Brazil \"President of Brazil\") and 26th [vice president](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vice_President_of_Brazil \"Vice President of Brazil\"), respectively, on 1 January 2023, in a ceremony held in the [National Congress](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Congress_of_Brazil \"National Congress of Brazil\") in [Brasília](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bras%C3%ADlia \"Brasília\"), beginning the third Lula administration. At the age of 77, Lula became the oldest president-elect to assume office and the only president in Brazilian history to serve two non-consecutive terms in office through the democratic vote.[[1]](#cite_note-1)\n\nOn 2 October, the day of the first round of voting in the [2022 general election](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Brazilian_general_election \"2022 Brazilian general election\"), Lula placed first with 48.43% of the valid votes, with which he qualified for a runoff against incumbent Jair Bolsonaro, who garnered 43.20% of the valid votes.[[2]](#cite_note-2) Lula was elected in the second round on 30 October, making him Brazil's first three-term president and the first since [Getúlio Vargas](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Get%C3%BAlio_Vargas \"Getúlio Vargas\") to be elected for a non-consecutive term. He was inaugurated on 1 January 2023.[[3]](#cite_note-3) In break with tradition, outgoing president [Jair Bolsonaro](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jair_Bolsonaro \"Jair Bolsonaro\") did not attend his successor's inauguration and instead left Brazil for the U.S. state of Florida two days before the ceremony.[[4]](#cite_note-4)\n\n[![](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Brasilia_Congresso_Nacional_05_2007_221.jpg/500px-Brasilia_Congresso_Nacional_05_2007_221.jpg)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Brasilia_Congresso_Nacional_05_2007_221.jpg)\n\nThe [National Congress of Brazil](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Congress_of_Brazil \"National Congress of Brazil\"), where the presidential [swearing-in](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oath \"Oath\") ceremony took place.\n\nThe presidential inauguration ceremony took place in and outside the [National Congress](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Congress_of_Brazil \"National Congress of Brazil\") building. The President-elect and the Vice President-elect paraded in a [Rolls-Royce Silver Wraith](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolls-Royce_Silver_Wraith \"Rolls-Royce Silver Wraith\") from the [Brasília Cathedral](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cathedral_of_Bras%C3%ADlia \"Cathedral of Brasília\") to the [Nereu Ramos Palace](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Congress_Palace \"National Congress Palace\"), where the presidential swearing-in oath took place during the joint congressional session.[[5]](#cite_note-5) The [Federal Senate TV channel](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TV_Senado \"TV Senado\") as well as major brazilian TV channels such as [TV Globo](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TV_Globo \"TV Globo\"), [Bandeirantes](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rede_Bandeirantes \"Rede Bandeirantes\") and [SBT](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sistema_Brasileiro_de_Televis%C3%A3o \"Sistema Brasileiro de Televisão\") broadcast the inauguration ceremony.[[6]](#cite_note-6)\n\nThe session was opened by [Senator Rodrigo Pacheco](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rodrigo_Pacheco_(politician) \"Rodrigo Pacheco (politician)\"), President of the National Congress (in his capacity as [President of the Federal Senate](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_the_Federal_Senate_(Brazil) \"President of the Federal Senate (Brazil)\")), who declared a moment of silence for [Pelé](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pel%C3%A9 \"Pelé\") and [Pope Benedict XVI](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pope_Benedict_XVI \"Pope Benedict XVI\"), both of whom had died in the week prior. After the playing of the [National anthem of Brazil](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_anthem_of_Brazil \"National anthem of Brazil\"), Lula and Alckmin took their respective oaths of office, after which [First Secretary of the Chamber of Deputies](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Secretary_of_the_Chamber_of_Deputies_(Brazil) \"First Secretary of the Chamber of Deputies (Brazil)\") [Luciano Bivar](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luciano_Bivar \"Luciano Bivar\") read out the official record of the election and oaths of office. The record was signed by Lula, Alckmin, Pacheco, Bivar, [Arthur Lira](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arthur_Lira \"Arthur Lira\") ([President of the Chamber of Deputies](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_the_Chamber_of_Deputies_(Brazil) \"President of the Chamber of Deputies (Brazil)\")), [Minister](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supreme_Federal_Court \"Supreme Federal Court\") [Rosa Weber](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosa_Weber \"Rosa Weber\") ([President of the Supreme Federal Court](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_the_Supreme_Federal_Court \"President of the Supreme Federal Court\")) and [Augusto Aras](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Augusto_Aras \"Augusto Aras\") ([Prosecutor General](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prosecutor_General_of_the_Republic_(Brazil) \"Prosecutor General of the Republic (Brazil)\")). Lula made a speech to accept his inauguration, and Pacheco subsequently spoke to affirm the commitment of Congress to working with the executive branch on key issues, after which he closed the session.\n\nGuests in attendance at the joint session included former presidents [José Sarney](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jos%C3%A9_Sarney \"José Sarney\") and [Dilma Rousseff](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dilma_Rousseff \"Dilma Rousseff\"), [Minister](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supreme_Federal_Court \"Supreme Federal Court\") [Alexandre de Moraes](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexandre_de_Moraes \"Alexandre de Moraes\") (President of the [Superior Electoral Court](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superior_Electoral_Court \"Superior Electoral Court\")), Minister Maria Thereza de Assis Moura (President of the [Superior Court of Justice](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superior_Court_of_Justice_(Brazil) \"Superior Court of Justice (Brazil)\")), and Minister Lélio Bentes Corrêa (President of the [Superior Labor Court](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superior_Labor_Court \"Superior Labor Court\")).\n\nAfter the joint session, Lula, Alckmin and their spouses were paraded to the [Palácio do Planalto](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pal%C3%A1cio_do_Planalto \"Palácio do Planalto\"), where they were joined at the ramp by several individuals selected from among Lula's voters by the [presidential transition cabinet](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_presidential_transition_of_Luiz_In%C3%A1cio_Lula_da_Silva \"Second presidential transition of Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva\") to represent the diversity of Brazil:[[7]](#cite_note-7)\n\n* Chief [Raoni Metuktire](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raoni_Metuktire \"Raoni Metuktire\"), an indigenous leader and an activist for conservation of the Amazon\n* Aline Sousa, a 33-year-old garbage collector and member of the National Movement of Waste Pickers (MNCR)\n* Francisco Carlos do Nascimento e Silva, a 10-year-old swimmer from the outskirts of [São Paulo](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S%C3%A3o_Paulo \"São Paulo\")\n* [Ivan Baron](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivan_Baron_(activist) \"Ivan Baron (activist)\"), a social media personality and a social justice activist from [Rio Grande do Norte](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rio_Grande_do_Norte \"Rio Grande do Norte\")\n* Murilo de Quadros Jesus, a teacher from [Curitiba](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Curitiba \"Curitiba\")\n* Jucimara Fausto dos Santos, a cook for the Association of Employees of the [State University of Maringá](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_University_of_Maring%C3%A1 \"State University of Maringá\") and a member of the [Free Lula movement](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Free_Lula_movement \"Free Lula movement\")\n* Wesley Viesba Rodrigues Rocha, a metallurgist\n* Flávio Pereira, an artisan and a member of the [Free Lula movement](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Free_Lula_movement \"Free Lula movement\")\n\nAs Bolsonaro was not in attendance, the presidential sash was handed among the aforementioned and placed on Lula's shoulder by Sousa. Lula, Alckmin and their spouses then walked to the podium of the palace where Lula spoke to the nation. After the speech, the four then walked inside the building again to receive foreign state delegations. Afterward, Lula publicly signed executive orders rescinding several decrees from the Bolsonaro administration, including re-establishing gun control, restoring the [Bolsa Família](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bolsa_Fam%C3%ADlia \"Bolsa Família\") program, creating an exclusive cabinet for matters involving indigenous and minority affairs, combatting de-forestation in the Amazon and illegal mining, restoring the [Amazon Fund](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Amazon_Fund \"The Amazon Fund\") and [civil society](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Civil_society \"Civil society\") participation in the National Environment Council (Conama).[[8]](#cite_note-8)\n\n| External videos | |\n| --- | --- |\n| Lula's Presidential Inauguration Ceremony | |\n| [YouTube logo](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:YouTube_2024.svg)     via [YouTube](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/YouTube \"YouTube\") | |\n| [video icon](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Nuvola_apps_kaboodle.svg) [Live: Presidential Inauguration Ceremony 2023](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ga2lkpGYNng) (1 January 2023), by [TV Brasil Gov](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TV_Brasil \"TV Brasil\") (in [Portuguese](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brazilian_Portuguese \"Brazilian Portuguese\")) | |\n\nLula's third inauguration was attended by the largest number of foreign leaders at a presidential inauguration in Brazil's history, beating the then record held by Lula himself in [his first inauguration](https://en.wikipedia.org/wik\n\n<error>Content truncated. Call the fetch tool with a start_index of 12000 to get more content.</error>"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
