{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"fetch","tool":"fetch","arguments":{"max_length":12000,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/8_January_Bras%C3%ADlia_attacks"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Contents of https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/8_January_Bras%C3%ADlia_attacks:\n| 8 January Brasília attacks | |\n| --- | --- |\n| Part of the [2022–2023 Brazilian election protests](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022%E2%80%932023_Brazilian_election_protests \"2022–2023 Brazilian election protests\") and the [2022 Brazilian coup plot](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Brazilian_coup_plot \"2022 Brazilian coup plot\") | |\n| From top to bottom, left to right:  * Crowd outside of the [National Congress Palace](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Congress_Palace \"National Congress Palace\") during the attack * Protesters outside of the [Supreme Federal Court Palace](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supreme_Federal_Court_Palace \"Supreme Federal Court Palace\") * Rioters destroying furniture inside the [Palácio do Planalto](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pal%C3%A1cio_do_Planalto \"Palácio do Planalto\") * Police barriers broken through by rioters nearby the National Congress building | |\n| Date | 8 January 2023; 3 years ago |\n| Location | [Praça dos Três Poderes](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pra%C3%A7a_dos_Tr%C3%AAs_Poderes \"Praça dos Três Poderes\"), Brasília, Federal District, Brazil  [15°48′03″S 47°51′41″W﻿ / ﻿15.80083°S 47.86139°W](https://geohack.toolforge.org/geohack.php?pagename=8_January_Bras%C3%ADlia_attacks&params=15_48_03_S_47_51_41_W_) |\n| Caused by | * False allegations of electoral fraud in the [2022 Brazilian general election](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Brazilian_general_election \"2022 Brazilian general election\") promoted by former President [Jair Bolsonaro](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jair_Bolsonaro \"Jair Bolsonaro\") and his allies[[1]](#cite_note-army_suppress-1) * Denial of the [2022 presidential election](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Brazilian_general_election \"2022 Brazilian general election\") results * [Far-right extremism](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Far-right_extremism \"Far-right extremism\") in Brazil |\n| Goals | * Pressure military and government officials to instigate a coup d'état against President [Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luiz_In%C3%A1cio_Lula_da_Silva \"Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva\")'s government[[2]](#cite_note-NPRMilitaryCall-2) * Reinstate Jair Bolsonaro as [President of Brazil](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_Brazil \"President of Brazil\")[[3]](#cite_note-3)[[4]](#cite_note-4) |\n| Methods | * [Protest](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Protest \"Protest\"): picketing, political demonstration * [Civil disorder](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Civil_disorder \"Civil disorder\"): assault, rioting, looting, vandalism, attempted arson * [Political subversion](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Subversion \"Subversion\"): [propaganda (big lie)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_lie \"Big lie\"), conspiracy, [sedition](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sedition \"Sedition\"), intimidation, [attacking a legislature](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_attacks_on_legislatures \"List of attacks on legislatures\") |\n| Result | [Coup attempt failed](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022%E2%80%932023_Brazilian_coup_plot \"2022–2023 Brazilian coup plot\")  * Riot suppressed; all targeted buildings cleared * Detainment *en masse* of rioters by law enforcement * Dozens of security officials assaulted, at least 44 hospitalized * Several protesters injured, 40+ hospitalized * Extensive damage to the targeted buildings and surrounding area, at least R$16 million for repairs and security measures * Several art pieces stolen or damaged * Declaration of federal intervention on the [Federal District](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Federal_District_(Brazil) \"Federal District (Brazil)\") for the remainder of January * [Supreme Federal Court](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supreme_Federal_Court \"Supreme Federal Court\") order suspends [Ibaneis Rocha](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ibaneis_Rocha \"Ibaneis Rocha\") as governor of the Federal District for 90 days * Installation of the [8 January CPMI](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/8_January_CPMI \"8 January CPMI\") in the National Congress * Jair Bolsonaro and his running mate [Walter Braga Netto](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walter_Braga_Netto \"Walter Braga Netto\") are declared ineligible following an Electoral Court ruling on June 30[[5]](#cite_note-5) * Bolsonaro and his close allies are [sentenced by the Supreme Court](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AP_2668 \"AP 2668\") on 11 September 2025 for their role in a [coup plot](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022%E2%80%932023_Brazilian_coup_plot \"2022–2023 Brazilian coup plot\") against then president-elect Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva[[6]](#cite_note-6) |\n| Parties | |\n| |  |  | | --- | --- | | Pro-[Bolsonaro](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jair_Bolsonaro \"Jair Bolsonaro\") protesters   * Armed protesters[[7]](#cite_note-7) * Police and military personnel (both active and reservists)[[8]](#cite_note-folha_military-8) * Former [Jair Bolsonaro government](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Presidency_of_Jair_Bolsonaro \"Presidency of Jair Bolsonaro\") members and politicians[[8]](#cite_note-folha_military-8)[[9]](#cite_note-9) * Various far-right groups and movements[[10]](#cite_note-10) | * [Federal](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Government_of_Brazil \"Government of Brazil\") and [state](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Federal_District_(Brazil) \"Federal District (Brazil)\") government forces   + [Congress](https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Departamento%20de%20Pol%C3%ADcia%20Legislativa \"pt:Departamento de Polícia Legislativa\"), Supreme Court and [Senate](https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pol%C3%ADcia%20do%20Senado%20Federal \"pt:Polícia do Senado Federal\") security[[11]](#cite_note-SenatePolice-11)   + [Federal](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Federal_Police_of_Brazil \"Federal Police of Brazil\") and [Federal Highway](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Federal_Highway_Police_(Brazil) \"Federal Highway Police (Brazil)\") police     - [Tactical Operations](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Comando_de_Opera%C3%A7%C3%B5es_T%C3%A1ticas \"Comando de Operações Táticas\") and [Aviation](https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coordena%C3%A7%C3%A3o%20de%20Avia%C3%A7%C3%A3o%20Operacional \"pt:Coordenação de Aviação Operacional\") commands[[12]](#cite_note-COT-12)   + [Military Police](https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pol%C3%ADcia%20Militar%20do%20Distrito%20Federal \"pt:Polícia Militar do Distrito Federal\")[[13]](#cite_note-13)     - [Riot control](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riot_police \"Riot police\") unit[[14]](#cite_note-NYtimesriot-14)     - [Special Operations Battalion](https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Batalh%C3%A3o%20de%20Opera%C3%A7%C3%B5es%20Especiais%20(PMDF) \"pt:Batalhão de Operações Especiais (PMDF)\")[[14]](#cite_note-NYtimesriot-14)   + [Civil Police](https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pol%C3%ADcia%20Civil%20do%20Distrito%20Federal \"pt:Polícia Civil do Distrito Federal\")     - Special Operations Division[[14]](#cite_note-NYtimesriot-14)   + [Institutional Security Bureau](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Institutional_Security_Bureau \"Institutional Security Bureau\")[[15]](#cite_note-UolGsi-15)[[16]](#cite_note-CNNDias-16)   + [National Public Security Force](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Public_Security_Force \"National Public Security Force\")[[17]](#cite_note-17)   + [Brazilian Armed Forces](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brazilian_Armed_Forces \"Brazilian Armed Forces\")     - [Brazilian Army](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brazilian_Army \"Brazilian Army\")[[18]](#cite_note-NYTimes8Jan2023-18) | | |\n| Lead figures | |\n| *No known organised leadership*  * [Lula da Silva](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luiz_In%C3%A1cio_Lula_da_Silva \"Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva\") * [Flávio Dino](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fl%C3%A1vio_Dino \"Flávio Dino\") * [Gonçalves Dias](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marco_Edson_Gon%C3%A7alves_Dias \"Marco Edson Gonçalves Dias\") * [Ibaneis Rocha](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ibaneis_Rocha \"Ibaneis Rocha\") | |\n| Number | |\n| |  |  | | --- | --- | | 5,000+[[19]](#cite_note-rochatorres-19) | Unknown | | |\n| Casualties | |\n| Injuries | 80+ (~40 rioters and at least 44 security agents), 6 in serious condition (including 2 in need of surgery)[[20]](#cite_note-20) |\n| Arrested | 1,430+ (according to the Supreme Court)[[21]](#cite_note-arrestsBBC-21)[[22]](#cite_note-detentions-22) |\n| Damage | at least $16 million [BRL](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brazilian_real \"Brazilian real\")[[22]](#cite_note-detentions-22) |\n| [Detained](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Detention_(imprisonment) \"Detention (imprisonment)\") | 2,100+ (at least 1,920 between 8–9 January)[[21]](#cite_note-arrestsBBC-21)[[22]](#cite_note-detentions-22)[[23]](#cite_note-Moraes-23) |\n| [Charged](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Criminal_charge \"Criminal charge\") | 86 (23 criminally charged, 65 awaiting judgement)[[21]](#cite_note-arrestsBBC-21)[[22]](#cite_note-detentions-22)[[24]](#cite_note-24) |\n\nOn 8 January 2023, following the defeat of then-president [Jair Bolsonaro](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jair_Bolsonaro \"Jair Bolsonaro\") in the [2022 Brazilian general election](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Brazilian_general_election \"2022 Brazilian general election\") and the [inauguration](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Third_inauguration_of_Luiz_In%C3%A1cio_Lula_da_Silva \"Third inauguration of Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva\") of his successor [Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luiz_In%C3%A1cio_Lula_da_Silva \"Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva\"), a mob of Bolsonaro's supporters attacked Brazil's federal government buildings in the capital, [Brasília](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bras%C3%ADlia \"Brasília\"). The mob invaded and caused deliberate damage to the [Supreme Federal Court](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supreme_Federal_Court \"Supreme Federal Court\"), the [National Congress Palace](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Congress_Palace \"National Congress Palace\") and the [Planalto Presidential Palace](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Planalto_Presidential_Palace \"Planalto Presidential Palace\") in the [Praça dos Três Poderes](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pra%C3%A7a_dos_Tr%C3%AAs_Poderes \"Praça dos Três Poderes\") (English: *Three Powers Square* or *Three Branches of Government*[[25]](#cite_note-25)), seeking to violently overthrow the democratically elected president Lula, who had been inaugurated on 1 January. Many rioters said their purpose was to spur military leaders to launch a \"[military intervention](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1964_Brazilian_coup_d'%C3%A9tat \"1964 Brazilian coup d'état\")\" (related to a misinterpretation of the 142nd article of the [Brazilian constitution](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitution_of_Brazil \"Constitution of Brazil\") and a [euphemism](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euphemism \"Euphemism\") for a [coup d'état](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coup_d'%C3%A9tat \"Coup d'état\")) and disrupt the democratic [transition of power](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peaceful_transition_of_power \"Peaceful transition of power\").[[26]](#cite_note-26) The event is sometimes called the Bolsonarist uprising.[[27]](#cite_note-27)\n\nAt the time of the riots, neither Lula nor Bolsonaro were in Brasília: Lula was in [Araraquara](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Araraquara \"Araraquara\"), a city in the countryside of [São Paulo](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S%C3%A3o_Paulo_(state) \"São Paulo (state)\"), with mayor [Edinho Silva](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edinho_Silva \"Edinho Silva\") and ministers [Luiz Marinho](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luiz_Marinho \"Luiz Marinho\"), [Jader Barbalho Filho](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jader_Barbalho_Filho \"Jader Barbalho Filho\") and [Waldez Góes](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waldez_G%C3%B3es \"Waldez Góes\"), surveying the city after heavy rains in the municipality;[[28]](#cite_note-28) Bolsonaro was in [Orlando, Florida](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orlando,_Florida \"Orlando, Florida\"), where he had been since the last days of 2022, even before the end of his term.[[29]](#cite_note-29)\n\nThe attack occurred a week after Lula's inauguration and followed several weeks of unrest fr\n\n<error>Content truncated. Call the fetch tool with a start_index of 12000 to get more content.</error>"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
