nd tax reform.* Covington 2023/06 article, Domestic Policy Priorities section. **Locator:** Covington article. **Period fit:** 2023; **ruler attribution:** Lula-attributed appointment; **role:** positive (professional, continuity-anchored); **lenses:** 5B.2, 5B.5, 5B.7; **confidence:** medium_high.\n\n- **5B-ECON-04** — *Lula and his team were repeating the \"2003 playbook\": conservative fiscal/monetary policy + strong social policy for the poor + state-owned company role; risk of diminished returns given a more conservative Congress.* Covington 2023/06 article, \"The President's Playbook and its Limits\" section. **Locator:** Covington article. **Period fit:** 2023; **ruler attribution:** Lula-attributed; **role:** mixed (strategy choice); **lenses:** 5B.1, 5B.2, 5B.3, 5B.7, 5B.10; **confidence:** medium_high.\n\n- **5B-ECON-05** — *Bolsa Família was restored in January 2023 by executive order on inauguration day, with a minimum benefit of BRL 600 (raised to BRL 600 with additional BRL 150 per child under 6) — the social-policy expansion is one of Lula's signature 2023 commitments.* Confirmed via Covington context and the Lula biography page (gov.br/planalto/en/composition/biography-president-of-the-republic), plus France 24 inauguration coverage. **Locator:** Gov.br Planalto biography page; France 24 inauguration article. **Period fit:** 1 January 2023; **ruler attribution:** Lula-attributed; **role:** positive (welfare expansion, included in fiscal framework); **lenses:** 5B.1, 5B.6, 5B.8, 5B.9, 5B.10; **confidence:** medium_high (gov.br is the official site, primary source for the act; France 24 corroborates the framing).\n\n- **5B-ECON-06** — *Deforestation in the Amazon dropped 49 % from January–October 2023 versus the same period in 2022 (4,776 km² cleared in 2023 vs. ~9,400 km² in 2022). Cerrado deforestation, however, rose 34 % over the same period to 6,802 km².* HRW Brazil chapter 2024, Climate Change Policy and Impacts section (hrw.org/world-report/2024/